\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Councilmember Howorth reported that she attended the League of California Cities Annual Conference & Expo earlier this month in Long Beach, where she gained insights on how to be more strategic in the future regarding the allocation of City funds.\line\line Mayor Pro Tem Franklin reported that he also attended the League of California Cities Annual Conference & Expo, where he participated in several presentations, including one on parking planning, which noted that fewer than 5% of people receive parking citations. He also shared insights from a presentation on Proposition 36, which was passed by a large majority in California. He expressed concern that fewer than 15% of individuals accused of theft are seeking diversion services, and of those, only about half are receiving them.\line\line Mayor Lesser reported that he also attended the League of California Cities Annual Conference & Expo, where he found several sessions relevant to current community issues. He highlighted a presentation on coordinating emergency response, which provided valuable insights into roles, responsibilities, and best practices for preparedness. He also attended a session titled \ldblquote Are Council Meetings Getting Harder? Here\rquote s How to Make Them Smoother,\rdblquote  which offered helpful reminders and strategies for effective meeting management. Additionally, he participated in City Attorney sessions, including one focused on the financing of large, multi-year residential projects. He found this particularly relevant for cities like Manhattan Beach that support new housing development, but face challenges related to state-mandated infrastructure requirements without direct City Council input.\line\line\pard Councilmember Tarnay reported that she also attended the League of California Cities Annual Conference & Expo, where her focus was on learning as much as possible in her new role. She attended sessions on emergency preparedness and best practices, explored how technology can enhance city processes, and had the opportunity to network with colleagues from other cities to gain insights into shared challenges and potential solutions for Manhattan Beach.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


